.TH SDL_HINT_WAVE_FACT_CHUNK 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WAVE_FACT_CHUNK \- A variable controlling how the fact chunk affects the loading of a WAVE file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WAVE_FACT_CHUNK \(dqSDL_WAVE_FACT_CHUNK\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The fact chunk stores information about the number of samples of a WAVE file\[char46] The Standards Update from Microsoft notes that this value can be used to \(aqdetermine the length of the data in seconds\(aq\[char46] This is especially useful for compressed formats (for which this is a mandatory chunk) if they produce multiple sample frames per block and truncating the block is not allowed\[char46] The fact chunk can exactly specify how many sample frames there should be in this case\[char46]
.PP
Unfortunately, most application seem to ignore the fact chunk and so SDL ignores it by default as well\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqtruncate\(dq - Use the number of samples to truncate the wave data if the fact chunk is present and valid\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqstrict\(dq - Like \(dqtruncate\(dq, but raise an error if the fact chunk is invalid, not present for non-PCM formats, or if the data chunk doesn\(aqt have that many samples\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqignorezero\(dq - Like \(dqtruncate\(dq, but ignore fact chunk if the number of samples is zero\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqignore\(dq - Ignore fact chunk entirely\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint should be set before calling
.BR SDL_LoadWAV ()
or
.BR SDL_LoadWAV_IO ()

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

